      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c540514d859d512a8d1d2f9|full_name}: I think this is related to the \"accidental\" deletion of a massive amount of avatars from the servers, including default public models. We were loading some public avatars from the menu last night and nobody, including the person wearing them, could see them. They just got the error robot, but I could see them fine. From what I could tell, I could see it because it was loading from my cache, since I don't clear it unless I have a problem. They couldn't see it because they had cleaned their caches and the avatar had been deleted, so they got the error robot.",
